 break","Pitch structure","Build your pitch","Peer pitch review"],"expected_output":"Test card (and results if already tested); Completed lean one-page business plan; Three-minute pitch with up to five slides or a one-page visual; Peer review notes and revised assumptions","assessment_notes":"DRAFT (V13.2 curriculum revision, 19 Nov 2026): full lesson plan with timed segments, activities, assessment and facilitator notes. Assessment: 4 questions or tasks, checked against the expected outputs. Needs approval by programme management.","is_approved":false,"source":"curriculum_v13"}, {"id":"708f0f85-2909-443e-b47e-314a2934f2ea","programme_id":"00000000-0000-0000-0000-0000000000a1","track_id":"2653cd8b-059a-4e92-a230-f8c874b397b7","week_no":2,"session_no":3,"title":"Understanding AI, AI tools and responsible use","description":"What artificial intelligence is, the main types of AI tools and what they are used for, and the principles of responsible and ethical AI use.","duration_minutes":120,"objectives":["Explain in plain words what AI, machine learning and generative AI are, and how a chat assistant produces an answer","Identify AI already used in everyday Kenyan life (spam filters, maps, fraud alerts, translation, customer-care chatbots)","Name at least six types of AI tools and a practical use for each","Complete three AI-assisted tasks and record what the learner checked or changed","Explain five principles of responsible AI use (honesty, privacy, accuracy, fairness, human responsibility)","Agree and sign a group AI use code"],"topics":[],"activities":["Welcome to AI Tools and track overview","What AI is and how it works","Types and uses of AI tools","Demonstration - three AI tasks and what needed checking","Stretch break","Your three AI tasks","Responsible AI scenarios and group AI use code","Knowledge check","Wrap-up and homework"],"expected_output":"AI task log with three completed tasks and checks; Signed group AI use code with the disclosure line format","assessment_notes":"DRAFT (V13.2 curriculum revision, 19 Nov 2026): full lesson plan with timed segments, activities, assessment and facilitator notes. Assessment: 5 questions or tasks, checked against the expected outputs. Needs approval by programme management.","is_approved":false,"source":"curriculum_v13"}, {"id":"73a7a9f1-7e68-4ef7-ad69-a6eb5e907a7d","programme_id":"00000000-0000-0000-0000-0000000000a1","track_id":"f7dd75da-6a76-4cc0-b544-063a8565f290","week_no":4,"session_no":8,"title":"Content showcase","description":"Present your creative project and portfolio, explain your creative choices, give and receive feedback, pitch yourself and plan your next 30 days of content.","duration_minutes":120,"objectives":["Present the creative project and portfolio clearly in three minutes","Explain at least one creative choice and one responsible-content choice","Give and receive feedback professionally using the rubric","Pitch themselves as a creator with the portfolio as proof","Write a 30-day content plan"],"topics":[],"activities":["Showcase set-up and expectations","Project presentations and questions - block 1","Stretch break","Project presentations and questions - block 2","Feedback round","Pitching yourself and workplace readiness","30-day content plan","Celebration and close"],"expected_output":"Presented creative project and portfolio (final project) with rubric score and feedback; Portfolio message and creator pitch; 30-day content plan; Written feedback given to two peers","assessment_notes":"DRAFT (V13.2 curriculum revision, 19 Nov 2026): full lesson plan with timed segments, activities, assessment and facilitator notes. Assessment: 3 questions or tasks, checked against the expected outputs. Needs approval by programme management.","is_approved":false,"source":"curriculum_v13"}, {"id":"810c6163-429e-4db5-b72a-b88bfd6e88cd","programme_id":"00000000-0000-0000-0000-0000000000a1","track_id":"f7dd75da-6a76-4cc0-b544-063a8565f290","week_no":3,"session_no":6,"title":"Graphic design, visual storytelling, branding and responsible content","description":"Apply graphic design fundamentals, tell stories visually in carousels and posters, keep content consistent with a brand, and use content legally and responsibly.","duration_minutes":120,"objectives":["Apply the design principles contrast, repetition, alignment and proximity, plus typography and colour basics","Use grids and hierarchy to lay out a poster and a social post","Tell a story across a carousel (hook slide, steps or before-and-after, payoff, call to action)","Create a content brand kit (colours, fonts, logo or signature, templates, voice, recurring series)","Explain copyright basics in Kenya, licences, Creative Commons, consent and model releases, and platform rules","Keep a credit and consent log for all content"],"topics":["Visual hierarchy","Consistent branding","Consent and credit for people, images and music"],"activities":["Recap and video results","Graphic design fundamentals","Visual storytelling","Content branding and consistency","Stretch break","Copyright and responsible content use","Design a branded post, poster and carousel","Peer critique and knowledge check","Wrap-up and homework"],"expected_output":"Content brand kit with three templates; Branded post, poster and carousel; Credit and consent log (started)","assessment_notes":"DRAFT (V13.2 curriculum revision, 19 Nov 2026): full lesson plan with timed segments, activities, assessment and facilitator notes. Assessment: 5 questions or tasks, checked against the expected outputs. Needs approval by programme management.","is_approved":false,"source":"curriculum_v13"}, {"id":"86656270-aaa1-472b-bda9-d1a65186e185","programme_id":"00000000-0000-0000-0000-0000000000a1","track_id":"5b634bd2-5008-4a74-b026-dc19413903a4","week_no":4,"session_no":8,"title":"Business pitch showcase","description":"Present an early-stage business concept and identify a realistic validation step.","duration_minutes":120,"objectives":["Deliver a 3-minute business pitch with evidence and a specific ask","Answer questions about customers, numbers and assumptions","Give and receive feedback professionally using the rubric","Pitch themselves as entrepreneurs and as employable young people using the project as proof","Write a 30-day validation action plan"],"topics":[],"activities":["Showcase set-up and expectations","Pitches and questions - block 1","Stretch break","Pitches and questions - block 2","Feedback round","Pitching yourself and workplace readiness","30-day validation action plan","Celebration and close"],"expected_output":"Delivered business pitch (final project) with rubric score and feedback; Business concept summary (submitted in DIRA LEARN); 30-day validation action plan; Written feedback given to two peers","assessment_notes":"DRAFT (V13.2 curriculum revision, 19 Nov 2026): full lesson plan with timed segments, activities, assessment and facilitator notes. Assessment: 3 questions or tasks, checked against the expected outputs. Needs approval by programme management.","is_approved":false,"source":"curriculum_v13"}, {"id":"8a1c572a-22f6-4d92-9408-cf320f22f655","programme_id":"00000000-0000-0000-0000-0000000000a1","track_id":"f7dd75da-6a76-4cc0-b544-063a8565f290","week_no":2,"session_no":4,"title":"Smartphone photography, lighting, composition and mobile video","description":"Take clear, well-lit, well-composed photos and short videos on a phone, and capture clean sound.","duration_minutes":120,"objectives":["Apply composition techniques (rule of thirds, leading lines, framing, angles, clean backgrounds, symmetry)","Use phone camera features (gridlines, focus and exposure lock, portrait mode, HDR) and avoid digital zoom","Use natural light well (window light, golden hour, avoiding harsh midday sun, simple reflectors)","Film stable shots in the right orientation using wide, medium and close-up shots and B-roll","Capture clean audio (quiet location, mic close to the speaker, avoiding wind and echo)","Shoot a five-photo set and the clips for their storyboard, with consent"],"topics":[],"activities":["Recap and hooks you found","Composition and phone camera basics","Lighting","Mobile video production","Stretch break","Capturing clean sound","Practical shoot","Peer review of shots","Wrap-up and homework"],"expected_output":"Five-photo set for the brief; Storyboard clips including B-roll and a clean audio clip (complete or in progress); Peer-reviewed shot checklist with a reshoot plan","assessment_notes":"DRAFT (V13.2 curriculum revision, 19 Nov 2026): full lesson plan with timed segments, activities, assessment and facilitator notes. Assessment: 5 questions or tasks, checked against the expected outputs. Needs approval by programme management.","is_approved":false,"source":"curriculum_v13"}, {"id":"8a5cdcac-0981-4a47-9e37-f929a17941e5","programme_id":"00000000-0000-0000-0000-0000000000a1","track_id":"f7dd75da-6a76-4cc0-b544-063a8565f290","week_no":3,"session_no":5,"title":"Video editing, audio and sound, captions and creative writing","description":"Edit a short video on a phone, improve audio and add music legally, write on-screen captions and post captions, and export for each platform.","duration_minutes":120,"objectives":["Apply editing principles (hook first, cut on action, pacing, jump cuts, sequences, minimal transitions)","Edit a 30 to 60-second video in a free mobile editor (trim, split, arrange, speed, text, audio, colour)","Improve audio (levels, noise reduction, voice-over) and use music legally (platform libraries, royalty-free, licensed)","Add accurate on-screen captions for accessibility and check auto-captions","Write a post caption using creative writing techniques with a hook and call to action","Export with the right settings for each platform"],"topics":[],"activities":["Recap and footage check","Editing principles and demonstration","Edit your video","Stretch break","Audio and sound - editing and legal music","Captions and creative writing","Finish and export","Screening and knowledge check","Wrap-up and homework"],"expected_output":"Edited 30 to 60-second video with captions and legal audio; Post caption with hook and call to action","assessment_notes":"DRAFT (V13.2 curriculum revision, 19 Nov 2026): full lesson plan with timed segments, activities, assessment and facilitator notes. Assessment: 5 questions or tasks, checked against the expected outputs. Needs approval by programme management.","is_approved":false,"source":"curriculum_v13"}, {"id":"8d817596-1982-4768-9f6f-509ec448a925","programme_id":"00000000-0000-0000-0000-0000000000a1","track_id":"2653cd8b-059a-4e92-a230-f8c874b397b7","week_no":3,"session_no":6,"title":"AI for productivity, business and automation, with privacy, bias and limits","description":"Use AI for everyday tasks and small business activities, understand simple automation, and manage privacy, bias and the limitations of AI.","duration_minutes":120,"objectives":["Use AI for at least four productivity tasks (planning, summarising, organising, drafting, spreadsheet help)","Use AI for small business activities (customer replies, product descriptions, simple market research, social posts) with checks","Explain automation (trigger, action, human check) and identify three automation opportunities in a workflow","Explain how personal data must be protected when using AI, with reference to Kenya's Data Protection Act 2019","Identify bias and limitations in AI outputs, including language and local-context gaps","Map a routine workflow and build a reusable prompt set with human checkpoints"],"topics":[],"activities":["Recap and time audit","AI for productivity and everyday tasks","AI-assisted business activities","Introduction to automation","Stretch break","Privacy, bias and limitations","Workflow map and reusable prompt set","Knowledge check","Wrap-up and homework"],"expected_output":"Workflow map with H, AI and A steps, data points and human checks; Reusable prompt set (tested); Updated prompt library","assessment_notes":"DRAFT (V13.2 curriculum revision, 19 Nov 2026): full lesson plan with timed segments, activities, assessment and facilitator notes. Assessment: 5 questions or tasks, checked against the expected outputs. Needs approval by programme management.","is_approved":false,"source":"curriculum_v13"}, {"id":"9f499c8f-488f-4042-9513-80724e43c372","programme_id":"00000000-0000-0000-0000-0000000000a1","track_id":null,"week_no":1,"session_no":2,"title":"Digital foundations, AI awareness and communication","description":"Work safely and professionally online, understand what AI can and cannot do, communicate clearly, build a professional online presence and pitch yourself in 30 seconds.","duration_minutes":115,"objectives":["Apply five rules of professional online conduct (email, WhatsApp, video calls) and organise a programme folder","Explain three things AI tools can help with, three limitations and why human checking is always required","Write a clear prompt and improve the output using verification and their own judgement","Write a professional message and an email with a clear subject, greeting, request and sign-off","Improve one professional online profile (LinkedIn, Instagram bio, WhatsApp about or Facebook) so it matches their personal brand","Deliver a 30-second self-pitch and give respectful feedback to a peer","Recognise common online scams and privacy risks and know how to respond","Confirm their specialist track choice with a reason"],"topics":[],"activities":["Recap and digital confidence pulse check","Digital foundations and professional conduct","AI awareness and prompt practice","Clear communication practice","Professional online presence and self-pitch","Online safety scenarios","Core module check and track confirmation","Reflection, digital safety checklist and next steps"],"expected_output":"Programme folder with the standard file names; Short professional introduction message created with AI support, improved and checked 