facilitator notes. Assessment: 5 questions or tasks, checked against the expected outputs. Needs approval by programme management.","is_approved":false,"source":"curriculum_v13"}, {"id":"a123acb1-7333-44ae-92fb-d190c9ebd22c","programme_id":"00000000-0000-0000-0000-0000000000a1","track_id":"5b634bd2-5008-4a74-b026-dc19413903a4","week_no":2,"session_no":3,"title":"Opportunity spotting","description":"Identify customer needs and business opportunities; distinguish assumptions from evidence.","duration_minutes":120,"objectives":["Identify business opportunities from problems, trends, skills and resources in their community","Describe a customer problem in terms of the job the customer is trying to do, their pains and the gains they want","Distinguish assumptions from evidence and list the riskiest assumptions in an idea","Plan simple market research using primary (observation, interviews, surveys) and secondary (reports, data) sources","Describe a target market and early adopters for an idea","Conduct a practice customer interview using good, non-leading questions","Write a one-page opportunity statement"],"topics":[],"activities":["Welcome to Entrepreneurship & Business and track overview","Identifying business opportunities","Understanding customer problems","Market research and target markets","Stretch break","Demonstration - good and bad customer interviews","Interview guide and practice interviews","Opportunity statement","Wrap-up and homework"],"expected_output":"Three community problems and an opportunity chosen with the filter; Interview guide (eight to ten questions); One-page opportunity statement with top three assumptions","assessment_notes":"DRAFT (V13.2 curriculum revision, 19 Nov 2026): full lesson plan with timed segments, activities, assessment and facilitator notes. Assessment: 5 questions or tasks, checked against the expected outputs. Needs approval by programme management.","is_approved":false,"source":"curriculum_v13"}, {"id":"ad880c63-14d6-408b-8b